<title>USA: Montana Power Colstrip 3 seen up Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Montana Power Colstrip 3 seen up Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 750 megawatt unit 3 at the Colstrip coal-fired power plant in Montana should be back on line early Tuesday morning after tripping off Saturday due to a tube leak, a spokesman for Montana Power Co said Monday.</p>
<p>The plant's unit 2 was also out of service for a few hours on Sunday because of an instrument failure but is now back to full rate, added spokesman Cort Freeman.</p>
<p>Colstrip's other two units were operating &quot;full-out,&quot; he noted.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau, + 1 213 955 6761</p>
